## resistor_ref -- CLOSED 2026-11-17

DRC 0, LVS "Circuits match uniquely". 24.58 x 37.40 um. 4 devices, 4 nets.
Generator `analog/bandgap/scripts/gen_resistor_ref.py` (checks before emit).

Three FETs in a row below the resistor, so neither supply bus crosses the
414 um of precision poly. 1.2000 Mohm from `res_xhigh_po_0p69`, 20 x
l=20.84, extracted l_eff 414.01 um.

## Bandgap core (SPICE verified, layout deferred)

Charge-injection error closed from 13.7 mV to **0.92 mV** spread over
temperature. The debug is worth preserving: three plausible theories were
wrong -- symmetric-Ron sizing, leakage, settling -- each disproved by a
measurement that moved the wrong way, before width-scaling confirmed
injection.

* TG balanced 1:1 made injection **worse** (14.6 -> 17.8 mV); the PMOS had
  been partly cancelling. A measured sweep found the null at Wp = 4*Wn,
  where a two-point extrapolation had predicted 65 against the real 40.
* Longer channels (L 0.5) made it worse by 25 mV -- charge scales with W*L.
* Switch sizing settled at `bg_nsw` Wn=1.25, `bg_tg` Wn=1.25 / Wp=5.
* PNP port order is **Collector Base Emitter** -- emitter LAST.
* Caps: CA = 4x50f, CB = 40x50f, CF = 4x50f, Cp = 150f, CH = 1p.

